          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of George Bernard Shaw</strong><br>\nGeorge Bernard Shaw was born on July 26, 1856, in Dublin, Ireland. As a young child, he grew up in a household with a great love for music and arts, which influenced his later works. Despite his informal education, Shaw developed a voracious appetite for reading. This self-education would be evident in his writings, which often showcased his wide range of knowledge and sharp wit.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Shaw's Career Beginnings</strong><br>\nShaw moved to London at age 20, where he started his career by writing novels that were initially unsuccessful. He turned to journalism and criticism, writing for various papers. During this time, he became a respected theater critic and a vocal advocate for social issues, which laid the foundation for his future as a playwright.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Activism and Fabian Society</strong><br>\nShaw was an active socialist and joined the Fabian Society, where he edited their famous tract \"Fabian Essays in Socialism.\" His political views often permeated his plays, where he criticized social injustices and championed personal integrity and individualism over societal norms.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
